    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The GPS trace for TRP-00514 (EV-GPS-00514) is clean: 133 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, so none of POL-RD-07(a)-(c) fires and the deviation may be established on the trace alone, with no corroboration required and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation. Taking the governing trace length of 11.75 km — not the trip record's rounded 11.8 km copy, which POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test — against the booked optimal of 5.1 km, the excess is 6.65 km, i.e. 130.4% of optimal and far above the 0.8 km absolute floor. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass and the excess also exceeds 50% of optimal, so the deviation is established and MATERIAL. The driver's own account ('traffic on the direct road was heavy so I went around') confirms the vehicle left the direct route, and it is tested against a traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else (POL-RD-13). The bundle's advisory, EV-ADVIS-00514-01, is MISSING — status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, no payload — so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the traffic assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The driver named no advisory evidence ID, so the absent artifact is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact: POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged and the case is decided on the money, not escalated. The driver-side argument that the missing advisory forces an escalation is rejected for that reason (POL-RD-13(1)). Nothing else excuses the excess: the chat log is empty so POL-RD-04 has no rider instruction to run on; no amendment timestamp is set and amended_optimal_distance_km is null so POL-RD-05 does not apply; the fare is METERED and the vehicle is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 do not apply. The refund is arithmetic. Under POL-RD-02: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 5.1 + 0.28 x 9.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 10.945; charged_total is 19.61; refund = 19.61 - 10.945 = 8.665, which is not de minimis (above 0.50) and is 44.19% of the charged total, below the 90% share that would make it a full refund. Rounded UP to the nearest 0.05 the refund is 8.70, and the remaining 10.91 of the fare stands — which already meets the rider's own 'normally nine dollars' benchmark. There are no ERP, toll, airport-surcharge or waiting-fee lines to correct under POL-RD-09, and no charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace or trip record, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral. Because the deviation is MATERIAL the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check must be run: deviation_flags_90d is 0 and 0/250 = 0.00, so neither limb of the pattern test is met — no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. The ruling rests on artifacts at weight 1.0 (trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown); the missing advisory is the only zero-weight artifact and it carries no deciding fact, so confidence is not capped below 1.0. Confidence 0.9."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.90,
    "explanation": "This ruling concerns trip TRP-00514 (Blk 605 Yio Chu Kang Rd to Bishan MRT), for which the rider was charged SGD 19.61. I find the route deviation established and order a partial refund of SGD 8.70.\n\nROUTE. The platform's optimal route was 5.1 km / 9.0 min. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00514; COMPLETE, weight 1.0; 133 fixes at 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, longest gap 0.0 s) records 11.75 km driven — and POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure, not the trip record's rounded 11.8 km convenience copy, govern the threshold test. The excess is 6.65 km, which is 130.4% of optimal and above the 0.8 km absolute test, so the deviation is established, and at over 50% of optimal it is additionally a MATERIAL deviation. The trace shows none of the POL-RD-07 defects (no gap over 90 s, no jump over 500 m, no sampling interval over 30 s), so it is not impaired, no corroboration under POL-RD-07(ii) is required, and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation route is not engaged.\n\nEXCUSES. The chat log for this trip is empty (0 messages), so POL-RD-04 has no rider instruction to run on. Neither pickup_amended_at nor dropoff_amended_at is set, so POL-RD-05 cannot run, and the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. Nothing reduces the excess. The driver's statement that 'traffic on the direct road was heavy so I went around' is an admission that the vehicle left the optimal corridor, but as an explanation it carries no weight: POL-RD-13 tests a traffic excuse against this trip's traffic_advisory and nothing else, and the only advisory in the bundle (EV-ADVIS-00514-01) is MISSING, weight 0.0, no payload. The driver named no advisory evidence ID in his own assertion, so under POL-RD-13(1) this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact: POL-RD-10(5) is not triggered and the case does not escalate. The driver's argument that invoking POL-RD-03 against the absent advisory identifier compels an escalation under POL-RD-10(5) is rejected for that reason — an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one, and a bare traffic excuse is weightless under POL-RD-08.\n\nMONEY. The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, and the fare model is METERED. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 5.1 + 0.28 x 9.0) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 10.145, plus the 0.80 platform fee = SGD 10.945 (no ERP, tolls, airport surcharge, waiting fee or promo). charged_total is SGD 19.61, so the refund is 19.61 - 10.945 = SGD 8.665, rounded up to SGD 8.70, leaving SGD 10.91 payable. At 44.2% of the charge it is below the 90% full-refund share and above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor.\n\nCONDUCT AND BILLING. Because the deviation is MATERIAL, the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check must be run, and it fails: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 (below 3) and 0 divided by completed_trips_90d of 250 is 0.00 (below 0.05), so no pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c). No ERP or surcharge line is charged, and the ledger reconciles line for line (base 3.80 + distance 8.85 + time 6.16 + platform fee 0.80 = 19.61), so there is no unmatched line and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral. The driver's note that the 6.65 km excess is below the 8.0 km absolute materiality limb does not assist him: POL-RD-01's materiality test is disjunctive (over 50% of optimal OR over 8.0 km) and the 130.4% limb is met, and materiality only triggers the POL-RD-06 check, which fails in any event.\n\nCONFIDENCE. Confidence is 0.90, capped by the artifacts that carry the deciding facts — the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown — all at weight 1.0. The missing advisory carries no fact and therefore caps nothing; it is named here for transparency at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
